earlier this week I had the chance to  sit down with forts of horizon 2 and  play through pretty much the first hour  of the game now this may come as a shock  but it's pretty fun actually it's a lot  of fun but let's get a little more  focused than that here are the three  biggest takeaways from my time with the  game I want to find out who's the best  driver  first it feels like much more of an open  world than forts of horizon-1 now it's  not just the fact that it's bigger it's  the fact that there's so much more to  the game than what you find on the  actual roads so let's say you're just  free roaming and you want to goof around  hey look it's a vineyard I think I'll go  destroy it and you can do that you can  ruin a poor winemakers entire livelihood  just because you wanted to see how well  a BMW z4 could spin doughnuts in the  dirt or because you wanted to take a  shortcut on the way to your next  objective or because you just wanted to  drive off a cliff but the real payoff to  all of this it's not goofing around sure  that's fun but let's remember that this  is a racing game now the payoff is in  the off-roading events these are just  insane driving through these big  expansive open fields as you trade paint  with other cars and race through the  trees it's a whole new dynamic from the  rally events in the first horizon which  tended to focus more on sticking to  pre-arranged dirt roads but this this is  off-roading freedom  second it's a much more customizable  game than the first horizon oh yeah  here's where we do the real serious  stuff see horizon 2 is the first of  these spin-offs to adopt the tuning  system from forts and motorsport so if  you're a hardcore racing fan not only  can you scroll through the difficulty  settings and disable all the assists you  can also get super granular with your  gear ratios your downforce and whatever  else you want to tweak on that new ride  of yours and on top of that there's this  whole perk system which lets you spend  skill points to unlock new abilities for  yourself like the first one that gives  you xp for banking skill chains so  between that the tuning and the driving  assists you should be able to add quite  a bit of personal touch to the whole  driving system and finally let's talk  about the story now if you know me you  know that the story was pretty much my  least favorite thing about the original  horizon it just tried so hard to be cool  to the point where it felt like some  marketing executives fever dream vision  of a music festival when I saw that  horizon 2 opens up with all these  cinematics naturally I got a bit worried  but I don't know the whole thing seems  like it's a bit more dialed back  compared to horizon one a few narrative  beats I saw were quick they they got the  point across they didn't overstay their  welcome and that's good but at the same  time I can't help but wonder why they  bothered with that stuff at all but you  know either way the story stuff was  pretty minor and didn't detract from my  enjoyment of the game  I can already tell that horizon 2 is a  lot of fun and I am totally ready for  the full release later this month  you  [Music]
 

